test.yaml:2:3: trigger "pull_request_target" is dangerous: it runs in the context of the base repository with a write token and secrets even when the pull request comes from a fork. use "pull_request" unless write access is required, and never check out or run code of the pull request [dangerous-triggers]
test.yaml:4:3: trigger "workflow_run" is dangerous: it runs in the context of the default branch with a write token and secrets, but processes artifacts and metadata produced by a run that a fork may control. consider a reusable workflow called with "workflow_call" instead, and never trust the artifacts or the event payload [dangerous-triggers]
test.yaml:7:3: trigger "issue_comment" is dangerous: it runs in the context of the default branch with a write token and secrets and can be started by anyone who can comment. check the permission of the commenter and never run code of the pull request [dangerous-triggers]
